ile" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/state.json" "file_sha256" "95e9b903228e412bab0e16d8a3e3c7698d075032390af8f46cb4dc0ce13f6e11"} {"question" "q-321898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the reference angle associated with the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-3}{-3\\sqrt{3}}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the third quadrant. So, we find the angle in the third quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/state.json" "file_sha256" "95e9b903228e412bab0e16d8a3e3c7698d075032390af8f46cb4dc0ce13f6e11"} {"question" "q-321898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c83e68e27887c9b817086ec5abfdcf4882c2088e2f49f1961901c05fac5e67b8"} {"question" "q-321898" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/state.json" "file_sha256" "95e9b903228e412bab0e16d8a3e3c7698d075032390af8f46cb4dc0ce13f6e11"} {"question" "q-321898" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/